; Links the versioned compatibility attributes (see plat_pub_versioned.cil
; from vendor.img — it declares (type gskserver_exec) and
; (typeattribute gskserver_exec_33_0), but NOT the link between them: it is
; normally generated by Microsoft's PLATFORM build process, which we do not have).
; Without this link the rules already present in vendor_sepolicy.cil
; (allow init_33_0 gskserver_exec_33_0 ...) never apply to the
; real init/gskserver_exec — init gets avc: denied on getattr
; /vendor/bin/hw/windows.services.graphics@1.0-service (likewise for
; rcmsvc/windows.services.rcm). Found and explained 15.09.2026, see
; docs/findings.md "continuation 28" (section "Check on a real WSA").
;
; EXTENDED 18.09.2026: the list now covers the FULL contiguous block of
; Microsoft proprietary types in plat_pub_versioned.cil (between the stock
; zygote_exec_33_0 and the first neverallow) — previously this file had only
; gskserver/rcmsvc/rcmtestsvc; sysprep_service and logcat_forwarder
; were missing, although sysprep_service is EXACTLY the central component of
; that whole day's diagnostics (SysPrepChannel/vsock handshake with the host).
; windows-allocator-hal_tmpfs is a tmpfs type without an exec variant, present only in
; file_type, not in exec_type (checked against plat_pub_versioned.cil, both groups).
(typeattributeset gskserver_33_0 (gskserver))
(typeattributeset gskserver_exec_33_0 (gskserver_exec))
(typeattributeset rcmsvc_33_0 (rcmsvc))
(typeattributeset rcmsvc_exec_33_0 (rcmsvc_exec))
(typeattributeset rcmtestsvc_33_0 (rcmtestsvc))
(typeattributeset rcmtestsvc_exec_33_0 (rcmtestsvc_exec))
(typeattributeset sysprep_service_33_0 (sysprep_service))
(typeattributeset sysprep_service_exec_33_0 (sysprep_service_exec))
(typeattributeset logcat_forwarder_33_0 (logcat_forwarder))
(typeattributeset logcat_forwarder_exec_33_0 (logcat_forwarder_exec))
(typeattributeset windows-allocator-hal_tmpfs_33_0 (windows-allocator-hal_tmpfs))
